 {"version":"2026-10-09T12:02:15Z","deployment_id":"dpl_HGMKB8eZ3jUGAMVCyqu3YCjPX9nY","sha":"ddc9c705604d9e0a7949e0ebf4cd41bad47135af","deployed_sha":"ddc9c705604d9e0a7949e0ebf4cd41bad47135af","previous_sha":"ec809c7400e59a59a087699c4ea2ebce4efbe738","commit_count":16,"invisible":false,"generated_at":"2026-10-09T11:56:11Z","generated_by":{"trawl":"sonnet","review":"sol","copy":"opus"},"entries":[{"id":null,"section":"headline","title":"Ask in chat replaces Dig deeper","body":"Dig deeper has gone from Glossary and Citations entries, the cards that appear when you point at a term or a cited work, Skim's term chip and the comment box. On your own articles, those cards and Skim's chip gain Ask in chat in its place, as do open ideas in Ideas. A conversation started from Glossary, Citations, Ideas or Debate shows a way back that opens that mode at the item it came from. Dig deeper answers you kept are still shown.","where":null,"links":[{"label":"Glossary, Citations and Ideas","url":"/features"},{"label":"the changes","url":"https://github.com/spideryarn/reading2/commit/afbe657abe8f2c0b966b0b0c2193df8145e70066"}],"commits":["e1adfed3a40bef476efae5114a309274b95a4f66","afbe657abe8f2c0b966b0b0c2193df8145e70066","0e4d4bd7b73bb0022dd938bcf95a148a8a528e9e","3f94640ebe5bbb12f9b30809a8d844c24e7b4640"],"provenance":{"sources":[3,4],"verdicts":["confirmed","corrected"]}},{"id":null,"section":"headline","title":"Guide greets you, and works with Live","body":"An empty Guide conversation in Chat starts with a greeting instead of a separate form: it repeats the reason you gave for reading, or asks for one, and a short answer can be kept as that reason. Guide also works with Live, the spoken conversation, and on your own articles a Guide command in the command bar opens it without sending anything.","where":null,"links":[{"label":"Chat","url":"/features"},{"label":"the change","url":"https://github.com/spideryarn/reading2/commit/86f0ef2245d7286745cbf74a02502a3051be6476"}],"commits":["86f0ef2245d7286745cbf74a02502a3051be6476","ae065df85672e483b3a87f756c5683c153b448c4"],"provenance":{"sources":[1],"verdicts":["corrected"]}},{"id":null,"section":"enhancement","title":"Skim adds a cue only when it helps","body":"New Skim routes give a cue, the short line beside a quote, only when it adds what the quote lacks: what a reference points to, the question it settles, or why it matters. Existing routes keep theirs until re-planned. Cues are smaller and explain themselves when you point at one, and the current stop has one unbroken bar.","where":null,"links":[{"label":"Skim","url":"/features"},{"label":"the change","url":"https://github.com/spideryarn/reading2/commit/bc5fc52e285cc0d926fbaa3d7ed3026f20c6099e"}],"commits":["bc5fc52e285cc0d926fbaa3d7ed3026f20c6099e","7225f245c0f326aab17b1d0a20edbd1a449e336e"],"provenance":{"sources":[5],"verdicts":["corrected"]}},{"id":null,"section":"enhancement","title":"Sharing is clearer while an article is added","body":"While an article is being added, its sharing section says it stays private unless you choose, offers a private link first, and asks you to confirm before making it public. The public tick box used to look ticked while still asking, though nothing was shared. The page no longer says your text was sent before the request is accepted.","where":null,"links":[{"label":"the change","url":"https://github.com/spideryarn/reading2/commit/269e21ba53f2758fe5ee18609f4bc5e198a57e09"}],"commits":["269e21ba53f2758fe5ee18609f4bc5e198a57e09"],"provenance":{"sources":[2],"verdicts":["corrected"]}},{"id":null,"section":"enhancement","title":"Skim's profile notice can be closed","body":"On your own articles, the Skim notice saying a route was planned before your profile last changed has a close button, so you can keep the route without planning it again. The notice comes back if the route is re-planned or your profile changes again.","where":null,"links":[{"label":"Skim","url":"/features"},{"label":"the change","url":"https://github.com/spideryarn/reading2/commit/127b4ba82e56625594f65d632f3d9eef8b311dab"}],"commits":["127b4ba82e56625594f65d632f3d9eef8b311dab","823e6c565d0f4c3abe0714eb0197ec2baf188728"],"provenance":{"sources":[0],"verdicts":["confirmed"]}},{"id":null,"section":"fix","title":"Live no longer sees hidden button text","body":"When you carried a typed conversation on out loud with Live, the earlier replies handed to the voice still held the hidden text that draws their buttons, which the voice could pick up and imitate. That hidden text is left out.","where":null,"links":[{"label":"the change","url":"https://github.com/spideryarn/reading2/commit/86f0ef2245d7286745cbf74a02502a3051be6476"}],"commits":["86f0ef2245d7286745cbf74a02502a3051be6476"],"provenance":{"sources":[6],"verdicts":["sol-found"]}}]}
 {"version":"2026-10-09T14:54:37Z","deployment_id":"dpl_3qcaTjhMnSTjvsHeN33NGPTNtgPy","sha":"527d0ae962389a607262734f7f59abcb57e06d2d","deployed_sha":"527d0ae962389a607262734f7f59abcb57e06d2d","previous_sha":"ddc9c705604d9e0a7949e0ebf4cd41bad47135af","commit_count":5,"invisible":false,"generated_at":"2026-10-09T14:51:15Z","generated_by":{"trawl":"sonnet","review":"sol","copy":"opus"},"entries":[{"id":null,"section":"headline","title":"Adding an article offers a public copy first","body":"When the address you add matches an article another reader has made public, and that copy is ready to read, Spideryarn asks first. You can read the public copy free, or add your own, which uses one of your article slots as usual. The same choice appears when you add an article from a link inside another one, and 'Add a private copy' on a public article goes straight to adding your own.","where":null,"links":[{"label":"The public library","url":"/read/public"},{"label":"the change","url":"https://github.com/spideryarn/reading2/commit/427a08c84798e2117e5b9a569f07239c280d754f"}],"commits":["427a08c84798e2117e5b9a569f07239c280d754f","09aeebabf07adc400821d52a5aa3a11dd3799905"],"provenance":{"sources":[0],"verdicts":["corrected"]}},{"id":null,"section":"fix","title":"Unconfirmed private links can be turned off","body":"If the reply to 'Create the link' never arrived, the Add page offered only 'Check again', so a private link that might be live could not be stopped from there. A 'Turn off' button sits beside it. A link still being created when you press it may switch on afterwards; the tip on the button says so.","where":null,"links":[{"label":"the change","url":"https://github.com/spideryarn/reading2/commit/10d0944fb3d526766e7c168991eefcad849e96cc"}],"commits":["10d0944fb3d526766e7c168991eefcad849e96cc"],"provenance":{"sources":[1],"verdicts":["confirmed"]}}]}
 {"version":"2026-10-09T19:11:38Z","deployment_id":"dpl_D9L7e5ugBCusggMgACwBcrgCcZo9","sha":"35a3660e6d2c8aef94f8c23d7e1a3a1efb1688cb","deployed_sha":"8bd1e67bd92a81f175bc4d19e5011193a50a0d69","previous_sha":"527d0ae962389a607262734f7f59abcb57e06d2d","commit_count":17,"invisible":false,"generated_at":"2026-10-09T17:54:07Z","generated_by":{"trawl":"sonnet","review":"sol","copy":"opus"},"entries":[{"id":null,"section":"headline","title":"arXiv papers show where each author works","body":"When you add an arXiv paper from its web version, the app reads each author's institution from the paper's own title block and shows it when you point at an author's name, and under Authors in the article's Metadata. An institution is kept only if it matches words in that author's own entry on the page, so some authors may still have none. Articles you added before this change are not updated.","where":null,"links":[{"label":"the change","url":"https://github.com/spideryarn/reading2/commit/7b5c5b885bd88f36e3d903ab05614ef568db5e91"}],"commits":["7b5c5b885bd88f36e3d903ab05614ef568db5e91","316be869bf13146d3f074b77bd57379b4ea0afd3"],"provenance":{"sources":[3],"verdicts":["corrected"]}},{"id":null,"section":"enhancement","title":"Quoted passages keep their maths and italics","body":"Wherever a panel quotes the article, a formula is drawn as maths and italics stay italic, where before you could see the formula's raw typesetting code and plain text. This covers Skim, Quotes, Ideas, Timeline, Search, Glossary, Debate, the cards that appear over links within the article, and the comment and chat boxes.","where":null,"links":[{"label":"Modes","url":"/features"},{"label":"the changes","url":"https://github.com/spideryarn/reading2/commit/3488ca19619c007b7236c7598429dcb4d0ec46f7"}],"commits":["ec92f91ea4c060f39b390f0c21b27056b4f5afba","3488ca19619c007b7236c7598429dcb4d0ec46f7","1cd753d1e0b440b979e02424cdba08cf185bc597"],"provenance":{"sources":[0],"verdicts":["confirmed"]}},{"id":null,"section":"enhancement","title":"In Skim, the open stop puts its quote first","body":"In Skim, the section heading of the stop you have open is smaller and in a softer grey, the small buttons beside it are plain outlines, and the prompt to go deeper is no longer in italics. The quote is the first line your eye lands on.","where":null,"links":[{"label":"Skim","url":"/features"},{"label":"the change","url":"https://github.com/spideryarn/reading2/commit/c91efceab76d164a0d891f4861c76d30e4b6099c"}],"commits":["c91efceab76d164a0d891f4861c76d30e4b6099c"],"provenance":{"sources":[4],"verdicts":["confirmed"]}},{"id":null,"section":"fix","title":"PDF reading warnings are kept and exported","body":"When you add a PDF, the app checks its own reading of the file and notes any passages it doubts. Those notes were being thrown away; they are kept with the article and included when you download an article with Export. They are not shown while you read, and notes from PDFs added before this change cannot be recovered.","where":null,"links":[{"label":"the change","url":"https://github.com/spideryarn/reading2/commit/14a38a261be0ed80eeb9de2e46bc3d40af885d92"}],"commits":["14a38a261be0ed80eeb9de2e46bc3d40af885d92","7c18ff5d102ebf5660e7e057ba47ca0794a0d5e7","56adcafa56cc6eb4b7753d40b662e6ab282f767e"],"provenance":{"sources":[1],"verdicts":["corrected"]}},{"id":null,"section":"fix","title":"Debate no longer repeats an interrupted web search","body":"If preparing Debate was cut off partway through its search of the web, the app started that search again on its own, sometimes more than once. It stops instead and asks you to press Retry. Debate is behind the Experimental features switch on your profile page.","where":null,"links":[{"label":"Experimental features","url":"/profile"},{"label":"the change","url":"https://github.com/spideryarn/reading2/commit/2fc3f547bfb3639b87e6d65696c080581af99e9f"}],"commits":["2fc3f547bfb3639b87e6d65696c080581af99e9f"],"provenance":{"sources":[2],"verdicts":["confirmed"]}}]}
